:{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.4 to v4.5.dev.custom_build [a210fe6db]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev (a210fe6db) - macOS Sequoia (15.4.0) - Single-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Max (Apple7) - Apple M1 Max (10 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen \"Single Window Mode\" is enabled, the \"hover help\" tips in macOS cannot be interacted with: documentation links cannot be clicked, and all mouse input passes through to the editor control below.\n\nThis seems to be a side-effect of `EditorHelpBitTooltip` setting flag `Window::FLAG_NO_FOCUS` on macOS.  I get get clickable links when building Godot with the line that sets the flag commented out.\n\nIf these are intended to require a modifier to click, pressing any modifier (Command, Control, Option, or Shift) while the popups is displayed dismisses the popup immediately on macOS.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. In the Script editor, hover over a documented identifier, (e.g. `_ready` in `func _ready() -> void:` to invoke the popup after a short delay.\n2. Attempt to click one of the eight links in the popup.\n\nWith \"Single Window Mode\" enabled, this fails.  With \"Single Window Mode\" disabled, it works as expected.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nI experience this with an empty project.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred